A||||17||fierosound||BORLA EXHAUST - last day - JUNE 30||||6||
Z||000000||fierosound||06-08-2000||09:58 PM||||From what I understand, after talking with Tim, the FIERO Borla Exhaust orders will be going in June 30th.  Tim WILL NOT be ordering any extra systems, only those that have already been paid for BY JUNE 30th.  He feels those who have already paid for the systems deserve to get them.  He may not bother with another order after this.<P>YOU CAN STILL ORDER PRIOR TO JUNE 30th TO GET A SYSTEM!<P>Check this previous forum to refresh your memory...   <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002112.html</A> <P>I know alot of the guys think $420 is too expensive for a Borla stainless steel exhaust system. I think that is not a bad price for the BORLA system at all!  If you compare the price of Borlas on other cars - prices range from $400 to over $1000!!!!  Also, compare that to other stainless systems for the Fiero.<P>Check out the price of this stainless steel exhaust system from Fiero Heaven.   <A HREF="http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroheaven.com/Exhaust.htm</A> <P>RS Motorsports also has a stainless steel exhaust system for US$680.  <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/</A> <P>Of course, there's always the Ocelot exhaust from The Fiero Store and GM's stock exhaust system to choose from as well.  I've looked through the Fiero Store catalog - stock cat back systems are $180, Ocelot aluminized pipe cat backs are $270. They aren't performance systems, but then, you're buying them because they are cheap.  <A HREF="http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.secureleadercom.com/fierostore/</A> <P>I haven't heard anything further from Fiero Shop regarding his stainless exhaust system, and he never stated his expected price.    <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.net/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroshop.net/</A> <P>At present, the Borla system is still the best priced of the stainless steel performance exhaust systems for the Fiero THAT I COULD FIND.  Borla is a performance system with proven engineering - why re-invent the wheel??<P>As I plan to upgrade to a 3.4L with headers, (already buying parts)I think the BORLA exhaust will "complete" the exhaust system very nicely...<P>See the system at:   <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A> <P>To order, email Tim at:  tim@fieroparts.com<BR>You can phone Tim at:  (207) 934-0103<P><BR>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 06-08-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 07-20-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 07-20-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||06-09-2000||11:24 AM||||<BR>Forgive my ignorance regarding exhausts, and my Fiero's is at a point that it needs replacement.<P>So, can someone please tell me why a Borla exhaust is better than a well built inexpensive exhaust system?<P>Is there a real, attainable, performance difference, or is it like the dog bone example "you could by a $5 roll of tissue, but does it clean better than a $1 roll?"<P>I am lost when it comes to the exhaust, please help claify this issue.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierosound||06-10-2000||12:07 AM||||See the sites below:<P> <A HREF="http://macneilauto.com/Borla.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://macneilauto.com/Borla.htm</A>     <A HREF="http://www.borla.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.borla.com/</A> <P>Also see the power graph of the Borlas when tested on the Dyno at  <A HREF="http://www.fieroparts.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroparts.com</A> <P>They're proven to help produce power.  If they're good enough for Mercedes, Porsche, BWM, Corvette, Camaro etc..  I'm happy we can even get them for the Fiero. <P>I haven't seen too many stainless steel mufflers around, or muffler shops having a sale on custom built stainless steel exhaust systems.<P>To each his own...  Some would be happiest with a Yellow '88 GT w/T-tops - some are happy with an '84 4-cyl coupe.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||12-31-1995||11:48 PM||||I'm running the Borla system on my 87 GT.  I got it for improved gas milage/performance. I'm getting 31-33 mpg on road trips with the five speed.<P>If you plan on keeping your Fiero, spend the money and get the SS exhaust.  You can go to Mr Midas and spend a few bucks and then next year go back and spend the money again.  They'll give you a "free" muffler, but the pipes fall apart.  Been there, done that.<P>If you can't afford to maintain the Fiero, maybe you should trade it in on a Geo or something real cheap and disposable.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||07-15-2000||11:53 AM||||anyone heard anything else on these?||||reg||10
Z||000005||88formula||07-15-2000||12:36 PM||||You can get the Borla exhaust at Dason Auto Concepts Inc. 908 W. Hyde Park Blvd Inglewwod, CA 90302<BR>Phone (310) 677-7185<BR>Fax (310) 677-2630 <BR>This is where I got mine. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||HYPTNOTiSE||07-15-2000||04:54 PM||||I've been running the borla exhuast for sometime now, and i have one complaint. It's not a true performance exhuast. The piping and all is the same as it was from the factory with 2 inch pipe. I'm going to modify my borla by taking the pipe from the end of the crossover pipe that goes to the muffler and have it duplicated in 2.5 inch stainless, and have the old one cut off and reweld the new one on. That way it'll be custom equal length headers to a 2.25 crossover pipe, to a 2.5 inch collector, to a 2.5 inch pipe to the muffler and dual 2 inch pipes comming out the back. <P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||07-15-2000||05:51 PM||||HYPTNOTiSE I think you are wrong about the Borla exhaust not being a performance exhaust. The Borla exhaust system has true mandrel bends and their XR1 racing muffler. The Borla exhaust dynoed at 7-horse power over the stock fiero exhaust on a 2.8-liter engine. Bigger pipes will hurt the low-end torque of your motor. The smaller 2" pipes promote higher exhaust gas velocity, which helps to scavenge exhaust gas out of the cylinders. It also has a nice low rumble like growl that does not boom and is not too loud.<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||fierosound||07-16-2000||05:48 PM||||88-<P>No longer available until they do another production run...<P>Anyway...  how do you like yours??  <p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 07-16-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||88formula||07-16-2000||09:44 PM||||Mine is awesome. Did Dason Auto say that they could not get you one? They told me that they could get more no matter if it was just one or twenty.||||reg||1
Z||000010||HYPTNOTiSE||07-18-2000||05:34 PM||||It's not really a true Performance Exhuast. It's a performance stock replacment. You said the piping is mandrel bent. So is stock. You say that it's a higher flowing muffler, true but you also mentioned that higher flow cuts out on torque, so wouldn't you be sacrificing torque for hp, buy swaping over stock?  I'm running a 3.2 liter, very high output engine, and i'm going to need more flow up top. So modifing the exhuast to match the output size of my custom headers is the way to go. <P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000011||HYPTNOTiSE||07-18-2000||05:36 PM||||I can't argue about how Freaking awesome the exhuast sounds however!!! I swapped from stock exhuast with cat, to borla run without a cat, and when i first fired it up it practically gave me a boner!<P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
Z||000012||fieroparts.com||07-18-2000||07:20 PM||||<P>||||reg||3
Z||000013||fieroparts.com||07-18-2000||07:48 PM||||Hello to all,  <BR>Let me see now??? Fiero Borla<BR>exhaust systems are avalable at  Dason Auto Concepts in CA.  I DON"T THINK SO!  We<BR>(Fiero Parts And Appraisals) have a contract with Borla they sell to US and ONLY US.<BR>This company in CA got our (by mistake)proto-type (we used to approve and test for sound and fit)<BR>this is just that a proto-type made up of many small pieces of pipe all welded together,<BR>this system was NEVER ment to go on a Fiero, because it has flash welds inside the pipes slowing the flow.  I feel bad for <BR>88 formula for buying this system.  This system will fall apart in no time at all <BR>and IS NOT COVERED BY BORLA.............  just a proto-type.<P>I dare anyone to call Dason's auto first thing in the morning and order one. after they tell you they CAN NOT get it, then call Borla at 1-800-927-5129 and if the salesperson is on the ball they will tell you to call<BR>207-934-1969 or 1-800-255-3437 Fiero Parts And Appraisals<BR>to order one.<BR>I put one of the last ones on my car and love it, sounds super and I picked up 10 hp<BR>easy and that's on a 4 banger soon to be replaced by a 3.4 in 3 weeks.  So to all that did not get one the first time around<BR>I'll tell you to get off the pot and get your order in, so we can get the order in.<BR>If you have one of these systems and do not like it, we will gladly buy it back, full refund inc. shipping I have 23 on a list that would kill to get one.<BR>thank you for your time.  please e-mail me if you have ?'s at  I do not check this page<BR>all that often....<BR>tim@fieroparts.com <P>Tim<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||88formula||07-18-2000||08:28 PM||||Fieroparts, flash welds huh, I think not! You gave me a good scare fieroparts but I'm positive that the exhaust I have is genuine Borla with no flash welding like you say. It is new and I'm positive it has never been used before. It came in a Borla box with the million-mile warranty card inside. It has the Borla chrome tips with ONE PIECE mandrel bent 2" tubing (NO FLASH WELDING) and it looks just like the one you have on your site except this one has the chrome tips. <P>I found out about Dason Auto in California by e-mailing Borla directly. Just to make sure that Dasson Auto can get another Borla exhaust like he said he could I am going to call him and post what I find on this thread.<P>Prototype exhaust yeah right! If I saw that this thing was used and made up of a bunch of pieces after paying $500 for it I would have been screaming at the guy in California to give me my money back a long time ago.<P>Here is a picture of the Borla exhaust I have. The piece in the back were the catalytic converter goes is a cheap pipe from the Fiero Store. The camera flash was on causing it to glare off the muffler but it does say BORLA on the front just like the one on fieroparts web-site.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/003_0a_2.jpg">  <P><BR>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-18-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||fieroparts.com||07-19-2000||08:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88formula:<BR><B>Fieroparts, flash welds huh, I think not! You gave me a good scare fieroparts but I'm positive that the exhaust I have is genuine Borla with no flash welding like you say. It is new and I'm positive it has never been used before. It came in a Borla box with the million-mile warranty card inside. It has the Borla chrome tips with ONE PIECE mandrel bent 2" tubing (NO FLASH WELDING) and it looks just like the one you have on your site except this one has the chrome tips. <P>I found out about Dason Auto in California by e-mailing Borla directly. Just to make sure that Dasson Auto can get another Borla exhaust like he said he could I am going to call him and post what I find on this thread.<P>Prototype exhaust yeah right! If I saw that this thing was used and made up of a bunch of pieces after paying $500 for it I would have been screaming at the guy in California to give me my money back a long time ago.<P>Here is a picture of the Borla exhaust I have. The piece in the back were the catalytic converter goes is a cheap pipe from the Fiero Store. The camera flash was on causing it to glare off the muffler but it does say BORLA on the front just like the one on fieroparts web-site.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/003_0a_2.jpg">   <P><BR>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-18-2000).]<P>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 07-18-2000).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>?  "All most  looks like the one our web site<BR>but without tips". IT IS you need to take a second look, this is the same one we used on a car for 100 miles to test. You have a one piece system right????? Borla made ONLY ONE and it was the proto-type.  The reason we made the change to a two piece system is it would not flex as much. I can see the many pieces of pipe in your photo, not as well as in your first photo many months ago? you live near Worcester MA right?  e-mail me your address and phone # and I will come down myself and prove it to you. Just because it came in a Borla box means zip, I sent systems back because they did not meet to our satisfaction and they all came back in nice new boxes.  I can't wait to see what you post next, I called Dasons the last time you posted you got a system from them and they said Borla no longer makes them, then I called Borla  Don at ext 217 They said they goofed in selling that system.  can't wait...<BR>This will put this to rest once and for all<BR>who the only one that can get these systems<BR>period..........<P>tim <P>||||reg||3
Z||000016||BellaFiero||07-19-2000||10:02 AM||||To heck with what the Dyno says. Do you realise what $400 bucks can do for your Fiero BESIDES an exghaust? Yeah, performance is important, blah blah blah. Then go buy a Ram Air Trans Am. I’m sorry, guys, but I think that’s nuts to spend that much money on an exhaust system. Mine cost me $12.00. Got it from U-Wrench It Salvage off a 1988 GT. A little bit of customizing  and old-fashioned elbow grease and !VIOLA! Makes my four cylinder sound and look all the better.  As far as this "No, I am the only one who can get one!" "No, I can get one somewhere else!" "Can not!" "Can too!" ... um... who cares? If the man has a prototype exhaust, maybe he can get the damn thing manufactured and sell it for much cheaper than your genuine Borla system... for Pete's sake, I don't care about any name - I care about function. And $400 can get me alot more function than exhaust.  ||||reg||13
Z||000017||88formula||07-19-2000||05:19 PM||||Fieroparts wrote "? All most looks like the one our web site,<BR>But without tips.  IF IT IS you need to take a second look, this is the same one we used on a car for 100 miles to test. You have a one piece system right????? Borla made ONLY ONE and it was the proto-type. The reason we made the change to a two piece system is it would not flex as much. I can see the many pieces of pipe in your photo, not as well as in your first photo many months ago? you live near Worcester MA right? e-mail me your address and phone # and I will come down myself and prove it to you.”<P>The system I have is actually a two piece system just like the one you have. You could not have possible used this system on your car because it is virgin inside and out. There were no mounts welded to the system to hand it off the car either. I had to cut the old mounts off my original fiero exhaust and weld them onto the Borla exhaust system. The mounts I am talking about are the one’s that the springs hook onto. I am absolutely positive that this system is no prototype with welded pieces as you say it is so If you want to come and look at the system yourself then come on down and see. I will e-mail you my phone # and address.<P>I talked to Armando at Dason Auto in California today and he said that the Borla exhaust system is discontinued and that there is only one left. He said that several people have called him about it and that he is waiting for the first person that called him to get back to him. If that person does not get back to him than he will sell it to the next person that called. Who ever this person is this is the last Borla exhaust with the tips. <BR>||||reg||1
